// The 8888 SNORM, SINT and UINT layouts (blocker round 3): one fetch word each
// and two Vulkan formats apiece -- the packed A8B8G8R8 forms name the same memory
// order as their R8G8B8A8 twins, which is what the pair of rows proves. The
// values stay inside the signed ranges so a decode cannot clamp: 0x20, 0x40,
// 0x60 and 0x7f of 127 are 0.252, 0.504, 0.756 and 1.0, and the signed set adds
// its 128.
